   "basis": "read",
   "text": "Attending: turning the mind to a matter and dwelling on it. The operation is the same in every element: a person sets the mind on a matter and stays with it (meditate, ponder, consider, give thought, think on). It runs through four subgroups. What differs is the object (God's law and works, one's ways, a field, the toil of a life, the word), the mode (done, resolved, commanded, denied, lacking) and where it leads; those differences are kept as relating findings R1 and R4, not as separate behaviours.",
