   "key": "b2",
   "kind": "statement",
   "basis": "read",
   "text": "Taking something to be so: holding a view or supposition. The operation is a person holding that something is the case (suppose, think, judge, imagine) and, usually, acting on it. It gathers the supposing of the narratives, the view held and voiced, the view asked of a hearer, the view forbidden, and the view about oneself. Across the elements the view is tested by the verse and is often shown wrong; that recurring correction is part of what the elements share, so it stays inside the behaviour.",
