  {
   "key": "b3",
   "kind": "statement",
   "basis": "read",
   "text": "Reckoning and regarding: giving something a standing or worth. The operation is a valuation: counting someone or something as a thing (faithful, able, nothing, worthy, forbidden), and giving or withholding regard. It differs from B2 in that the result is a standing conferred, not a fact believed. Weighing what is said or taught (1Cor 14:29, Ecc 12:9) is the same valuing, applied to words. 'Once regarded' (2Cor 5:16) is this valuation by a standard that is then given up.",
