  {
   "key": "b4",
   "kind": "statement",
   "basis": "read",
   "text": "Reasoning: working a matter through by argument, aloud or within. The operation is argument: one ground set against another to reach a conclusion. It is done aloud with hearers (Acts), called for by the Lord (Isa 1:18), given as a defense (1Pe 3:15), held silently in the heart (Luk 9:47) and, in Rom 2:15, as reasonings within one person that accuse or excuse. The 'conflicting thoughts' subgroup is the inward form of the same operation, so it is gathered here and not made a behaviour of its own.",
