   "key": "b5",
   "kind": "statement",
   "basis": "read",
   "text": "Devising: forming an intent within and carrying it into the deed. The operation is planning: a purpose is formed inside and issues in an act (to kill David, to destroy nations, to afflict Paul, the worst against the psalmist). The meditating of treachery (Psa 38:12) and the imagining of harm (Psa 41:7) are the same operation under the words of other subgroups. The figure of conceiving and bearing (Job 15:35, Isa 59:4) states the same move from within to without.",
